{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to find the other root of the quadratic equation \\(5x^2 + 4x - k = 0\\) given that one of the roots is 2. Let's proceed step by step.\n\n1. **Substitute the known root into the equation:**\n   Since \\(x = 2\\) is a root, it must satisfy the equation \\(5x^2 + 4x - k = 0\\). Substituting \\(x = 2\\) into the equation, we get:\n   \\[\n   5(2)^2 + 4(2) - k = 0\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the left-hand side, we have:\n   \\[\n   5 \\cdot 4 + 8 - k = 0 \\implies 20 + 8 - k = 0 \\implies 28 - k = 0 \\implies k = 28\n   \\]\n   So, the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   5x^2 + 4x - 28 = 0\n   \\]\n\n","prefix_end":590,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,1477,279,1008,3704,315,279,79151,23606,17767,20,87,61,17,488,220,19,87,481,595,284,220,15,57758,2661,429,825,315,279,19703,374,220,17,13,6771,594,10354,3019,553,3019,382,16,13,3070,3136,7660,279,3881,3704,1119,279,23606,25,1019,256,8704,17767,87,284,220,17,57758,374,264,3704,11,432,1969,26553,279,23606,17767,20,87,61,17,488,220,19,87,481,595,284,220,15,59,568,3719,3696,10607,17767,87,284,220,17,57758,1119,279,23606,11,582,633,510,256,1124,9640,256,220,20,7,17,29776,17,488,220,19,7,17,8,481,595,284,220,15,198,256,1124,921,256,61242,7766,279,2115,24413,3108,11,582,614,510,256,1124,9640,256,220,20,1124,50853,220,19,488,220,23,481,595,284,220,15,1124,6383,550,220,17,15,488,220,23,481,595,284,220,15,1124,6383,550,220,17,23,481,595,284,220,15,1124,6383,550,595,284,220,17,23,198,256,1124,921,256,2055,11,279,23606,9044,510,256,1124,9640,256,220,20,87,61,17,488,220,19,87,481,220,17,23,284,220,15,198,256,1124,2533,17,13,3070,10253,279,2097,429,279,2629,315,279,19703,315,264,79151,23606,374,2661,553,1124,4080,59,37018,90,65,15170,64,11035,1648,1019,256,1752,279,79151,23606,17767,706,61,17,488,44241,488,272,284,220,15,59,70